course: dictionary
lesson: 11900
title: Budge: move a little, or change your mind
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning is right. «The box was so heavy that it would not budge.» Nobody could move it, not even a tiny bit, so budge means move a little.
explain: «She has made up her mind, and she won't budge.» Nobody is pushing her, so budge is not about moving a body. Here it means she will not change her opinion. When you meet budge, ask: is something moving, or is someone changing their mind?
explain: Budge is often used in negative sentences, like «won't budge» or «wouldn't budge». Those phrases tell you that something or someone is stubborn and refuses to move or change.
explain: On a sofa or bench, «Budge up, please» is a friendly, informal way to ask someone to move along and make room. You will hear this in the UK, Ireland and Australia. Ask a friend to budge up and you can sit down too.
fact: «Budge» means to move a little.
fact: «Budge» can also mean to change your mind or opinion.
fact: «Won't budge» means refuses to move or refuses to change.
fact: «Budge up» or «budge over» means move along to make space for someone.
fact: Budge is a verb: budge, budges, budged, budging.
exercise: «The old gate was rusty, and it would not budge.» What does budge mean? | Paint with bright colours | *Move, even a little | Fall down with a crash | Shout loudly
exercise: «Dad said no, and he would not budge.» What does would not budge suggest? | He was very hungry | He was about to dance | He moved into the kitchen | *He refused to change his mind
exercise: Ella says, «Budge up, please, there's room on the bench.» What does budge up ask? | Stand up and leave | Lie down and go to sleep | Hurry to the shop | *Move along to make space
test: «The lid was stuck fast and would not budge, however hard Sam pushed.» What is the best meaning of budge here? | *To move a little | To sing loudly | To fall asleep | To shine brightly
test: Maya's friend says, «Budge over, I want to sit next to you.» What does budge over mean? | Cry quietly | *Move along to make room | Jump up and down | Run away fast
exam: «Grandad wouldn't budge on the rule, so we all had to go to bed at eight.» What does wouldn't budge mean in this sentence? | *Would not change the rule | Would not go to bed | Would not stop laughing | Would not move the bed
